
## Commits

Subjects are Conventional Commits — `type(optional-scope): what changed` — and
{{#if huskyOwnsHooks}}`.husky/commit-msg`{{else}}`.githooks/commit-msg`{{/if}} checks that shape on every commit. What language you
write in, whether a ticket number rides along, and whether you use an emoji are
this project's calls: write them down here, and extend that hook if you want
them enforced too. The body is free — it is where *why* goes, and why is what a
diff cannot say for itself.
{{#unless huskyOwnsHooks}}

Hooks are per-clone, so a fresh checkout needs one line before they run:

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

`sveltekit-fsd init` ran it for the clone it was run in.
{{/unless}}
